// ─── CLAUDE REVIEW — 2026-07-02 ───────────────────────────────────────────────

review("2026-07-02-claude") = {
  verdict: "APPROVED architecture / REQUIRED corrections before build",
  approved: [
    "in-nucleus file read, no NATS, no new deps — correct pattern",
    "graceful degradation contract (None, never crash)",
    "integration points in operational.rs + main.rs — minimal diff",
    "R10-clean (deterministic read, no LLM in signal path)",
    "chain-format safe: canonical_hash v2 encodes metrics generically — new
     s1_clima field needs NO chain version bump",
    "deploy protocol R1/R2/R4 correct (build 108, stop→verify PID→start)",
  ],
  required_corrections: [
    "C1 SCHEMA (blocking): the spec extracts global.stasis_cos / global.algedonic_status
     / systems[] — NONE of these exist in the real bundle. Verified live on 101
     (2026-07-02T05:17Z): top-level keys = domain, ts, events[], algedonic_status,
     baseline{}, _received_at, _recv_count. Correct mapping:
       stasis_cos   ← baseline.global_stasis_cos      (f64, e.g. 0.293)
       viability    ← baseline.global_viability       (f64 — ADD this field, cheap and useful)
       regime       ← baseline.global_regime          (str, e.g. 'active')
       algedonic    ← algedonic_status  (TOP-level; letter code e.g. 'B' — do NOT
                       assume green/amber/red)
       refreshed_at ← _received_at fallback ts        (this part was right)
       systems      ← baseline.n_systems fallback events.len()  (rename field 'zones'→'systems';
                       events[] are per-L1-SYSTEM summaries, not zones)",
    "C2 PATH (blocking): do not rebuild the path from env DISK_ROOT with fallback
     '/run/vsf' — wrong location (real file: /var/lib/vsf/vsf_nucleus/, and /run/vsf
     is tmpfs + proved wipe-prone on 2026-07-02). REUSE the existing
     clima_bundle_path() from s4_operational.rs (move it to the new module or call it).",
    "C3 STALENESS: in the prose but missing from the code sketch. Implement it,
     reusing the existing S4_CLIMA_BUNDLE_MAX_AGE_SECS const (same check as
     gather_climate_context_safe, s4_operational.rs:150-163).",
    "C4 TEST (blocking): add #[cfg(test)] with a VERBATIM production bundle sample
     (capture from 101) asserting every extracted field. This review caught schema
     drift precisely because the spec was written from an assumed schema — the test
     pins the real one. Same philosophy as recompute_matches_real_nucleus_event.",
    "C5 DEPENDENCY DECLARATION: the reader depends on s4_clima_bridge.py, which is
     an UNDECLARED process on 101 (found 2026-07-02, see RECON-BIDIRECTIONAL).
     Before deploy: declare s4_clima_bridge (and s4_markov_bridge) in state.db
     components — the φ↑ chain must not silently depend on an orphan.",
  ],
  note: "The schema error would have made the reader return None forever — graceful
         degradation into permanent silence. Worth registering as a lesson: specs
         that name concrete fields MUST cite a live capture, not memory. (Same
         session-theme: claims need machine-checkable evidence.)",
}
